;; Zimbabwe public holidays 2004-2040: external gold for ZW.
;; Regenerate: uv run --no-project --with holidays==0.109 python -I scripts/generate_mena_holiday_gold.py ZW
;; :days lists every holiday as (YEAR MONTH DAY NAME); any other day is not one.
(
 :country "ZW"
 :generated "2026-11-28"
 :from 2004 :to 2040
 :note "Public holidays of Zimbabwe: the Public Holidays and Prohibition of Business Act [Ch. 10:21] Schedule by era (Heroes' Day the second Monday of August and Defence Forces Day the Tuesday from Act 17/2001; Youth Day 21 Feb from 2018, SI 143/2017; Munhumutapa Day 15 Sep from 2026, SI 148/2026) with s. 2(1): a Sunday holiday adds the Monday, and the Tuesday when 26 December is a Monday; the yearly General Notices and the SIs for polling and other days 2004-2027. 2008 and 2012 are gaps (ZW-SECONDARY). 2028-2040 are provisional."
 :gaps (2008 2012)
 :weekends ((nil 6 7))
 :sources
 (
  (:title "Public Holidays and Prohibition of Business Act [Chapter 10:21] (Act 19 of 1969, consolidated to 31 December 2016)" :uri "https://web.archive.org/web/20260417054800id_/https://zimlii.org/akn/zw/act/1969/19/eng@2016-12-31"
   :text "s.2(1): the Schedule days are public holidays, provided (i) when a public holiday falls on a Sunday the following Monday is a public holiday, and (ii) when 26 December falls on a Monday the following Tuesday is a public holiday. s.2(2): the President may by statutory instrument declare any day a public holiday. Schedule: New Year's Day; Independence Day 18 April; Good Friday; the Saturday between Good Friday and Easter Sunday; Easter Monday; Worker's Day 1 May; Africa Day 25 May; the second Monday in August and the day following (Heroes' Day, Defence Forces National Day) [para substituted by Act 17 of 2001]; National Unity Day 22 December [para substituted by Act 17 of 2001]; Christmas Day and the day following. Easter Sunday is NOT in the Schedule but the Minister's annual lists include it from 2009. No Saturday rule.")
  (:title "Electoral Act [Chapter 2:13] (Act 25 of 2004), s.38(2)" :uri "https://zimlii.org/akn/zw/act/2004/25/eng@2016-12-31"
   :text "Polling days in a general election are deemed public holidays for the purposes of the Public Holidays and Prohibition of Business Act. The Minister still gazettes a notice (e.g. GN 1345A/2023).")
  (:title "Public Holidays and Prohibition of Business Notice, 2017 (SI 143 of 2017)" :uri "https://www.veritaszim.net/sites/veritas_d/files/SI%202017-143%20-%20Public%20Holiday%20Declaration%20-%2021st%20February%20-%20Robert%20Gabriel%20Mugabe%20National%20Youth%20Day.pdf"
   :text "Declares 21 February every year henceforth a public holiday, the Robert Gabriel Mugabe National Youth Day (s.2(2)). First observed 2018-02-21. Called 'National Youth Day' in the lists from 2021.")
  (:title "Public Holidays and Prohibition of Business (Declaration of Public Holiday) Notice, 2026 (SI 148 of 2026)" :uri "https://www.veritaszim.net/sites/veritas_d/files/SI%202026-148%20Public%20Holidays%20and%20Prohibition%20of%20Business%20%28Declaration%20of%20Public%20Holiday%29%20Notice%2C%202026.pdf"
   :text "Declares 15 September every year henceforth a public holiday, Munhumutapa Day. First observed Tuesday 2026-09-15 (Veritas Bill Watch 35/2026). Not in GN 788/2026 (the 2027 list, published earlier), but applies to 2027 by its own terms.")
  (:title "General Notice 325 of 2004, Public Holidays in 2004 (repeals GN 137 of 2004) (2004)" :uri "https://archive.gazettes.africa/archive/zw/2004/zw-government-gazette-dated-2004-06-18-no-45.pdf"
